    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Extensible Software in the age of LLMs",
      "url": "https://jeremymorrell.dev/blog/extensible-software-in-the-age-of-llms/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49363668",
      "score": 164,
      "comments": 74,
      "author": "coloneltcb",
      "published": "2026-08-19T16:26:05Z",
      "bullets": [
        "LLMs shift software extensibility from rigid plugin architectures to dynamic runtime tool-calling driven by natural language intent and structured schemas.",
        "Modern systems increasingly standardize on interfaces like Model Context Protocol (MCP) and sandboxed WASM runtimes for secure LLM integration.",
        "Developers must implement deterministic API contracts, granular permission boundaries, and schema validation to safely expose application state to AI agents."
      ]
